answer:
If I were to throw such a dinner party, I would hope my guests would be comprised of the following figures:

Lev Tolstoy, the esteemed Russian author;
Helen Keller;
Albert Einstein, the famous theoretical physicist;
Akbar, the tolerant Moghis ruler of India;
Florence Nightingale, the influential nurse;  
Isaac Newton;
Tutankhamun, the Pharaoh of Egypt;
Dante, the Italian poet from whom we have The Divine Comedy;
Aristotle, the Greek philosopher;
Nelson Mandela.
These people are iconic and influential figures who have significantly shaped history.

